PathwayData.put("data/grammar_vocabulary/units/L03U2.json",{"strand":"grammar_vocabulary","level":3,"cefr":"A2a","unit":2,"theme":"A Day to Remember","essential_question":"What makes a day special enough to remember?","lessons":[{"id":"GV-L03-U2-LS1","title":"We Visited the Rose Festival: Past Simple Regular Verbs","objectives":["Students will be able to form the past simple of regular verbs with -ed.","Students will be able to tell about finished actions in the past.","I can say \"We visited the festival\" and \"I enjoyed it\".","I can tell about a special day in the past."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من تكوين الماضي البسيط للأفعال المنتظمة بإضافة ed.","سيتمكن الطلاب من الحديث عن أفعال انتهت في الماضي.","أستطيع أن أقول We visited the festival وI enjoyed it.","أستطيع أن أحكي عن يوم مميز في الماضي."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"trip","pos":"noun","ipa":"/trɪp/","definition":"a short journey to a place and back","arabic":"رحلة","example":"Our class trip was to the science center.","image_id":"GV-L03-U2-LS1-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L03-U2-LS1-W01"},{"word":"picnic","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈpɪkˌnɪk/","definition":"a meal you eat outside, in a park or the countryside","arabic":"نزهة / رحلة طعام","example":"We had a picnic under the trees.","image_id":"GV-L03-U2-LS1-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L03-U2-LS1-W02"},{"word":"festival","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈfɛstəvəl/","definition":"a special time when people celebrate something","arabic":"مهرجان","example":"The date festival in Buraidah is famous.","image_id":"GV-L03-U2-LS1-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L03-U2-LS1-W03"},{"word":"visit","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ˈvɪzɪt/","definition":"to go to see a place or a person","arabic":"يزور","example":"We visited our cousins in Jeddah.","image_id":"GV-L03-U2-LS1-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L03-U2-LS1-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"We use the past simple for actions that started and finished in the past: We visited the festival last spring.\nFor regular verbs, add -ed to the base verb: visit → visited, walk → walked. The past form is the same for every subject: I visited, she visited, they visited.\nThere is no -s in the past: He played (NOT He playeds). Some spelling changes: arrive → arrived, try → tried, stop → stopped (see Lesson 4).\nverb + -ed: watch → watched, play → played\nsame form for all: I/you/he/she/it/we/they walked\nverbs ending in e → + d: arrive → arrived\npast time words: yesterday, last…, … ago, in 2020","examples":["I helped my mom yesterday.","We celebrated Eid at Grandpa's house.","The guests arrived at nine.","My brother painted a picture of the sea.","They watched the camel race last week.","Sara baked a cake for her friend.","We stayed in a hotel in Abha.","The teacher smiled at the class."],"common_errors":["✗ Yesterday I visit my uncle. → ✓ Yesterday I visited my uncle. (yesterday → past → -ed.)","✗ She walkeds to school. → ✓ She walked to school. (No -s in the past.)","✗ We are watched a film. → ✓ We watched a film. (No are with the past simple.)","✗ They arriveed late. → ✓ They arrived late. (Verb ends in e → just add -d.)"],"arabic":"نستخدم الماضي البسيط لأحداث بدأت وانتهت في الماضي: We visited the festival.\nللأفعال المنتظمة نضيف ed: visit → visited، والفعل الماضي لا يتغير مع الضمائر.\nلا نضيف s في الماضي: She walked (وليس walkeds).\nلا نضع are أو is قبل الفعل الماضي: We watched (وليس We are watched)."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “We Visited the Rose Festival: Past Simple Regular Verbs”. Let’s learn past simple affirmative of regular verbs (verb + -ed) together.","on_screen":"GV-L03-U2-LS1 | We Visited the Rose Festival: Past Simple Regular Verbs","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Listen to the start of “Our Day at the Rose Festival”: Last spring, my family and I visited the Taif Rose Festival. We arrived early in the morning. Look at the green words.","on_screen":"Last spring, my family and I visited the Taif Rose Festival. We arrived early in the morning.","visual":"Image GV-L03-U2-LS1-IMG01 animates gently; target words glow Leaf Green as they are spoken."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"We use the past simple for actions that started and finished in the past: We visited the festival last spring. For regular verbs, add -ed to the base verb: visit → visited, walk → walked. The past form is the same for every subject: I visited, she visited, they visited.","on_screen":"verb + -ed: watch → watched, play → played • same form for all: I/you/he/she/it/we/they walked • verbs ending in e → + d: arrive → arrived","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. I helped my mom yesterday. We celebrated Eid at Grandpa's house. The guests arrived at nine.","on_screen":"I helped my mom yesterday. / We celebrated Eid at Grandpa's house. / The guests arrived at nine.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “Yesterday I visit my uncle.” That’s not right. We say: “Yesterday I visited my uncle.” yesterday → past → -ed.","on_screen":"✗ Yesterday I visit my uncle.   ✓ Yesterday I visited my uncle.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"We visited the festival last spring.\" Is the visit finished? … Think! … Yes – it's in the past. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"We visited the festival\" and \"I enjoyed it\".","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can say \"We visited the festival\" and \"I enjoyed it\".","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: past simple affirmative of regular verbs (verb + -ed).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","نستخدم الماضي البسيط لأحداث بدأت وانتهت في الماضي: We visited the festival.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: Yesterday I visit my uncle. — الصحيح: Yesterday I visited my uncle.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أقول We visited the festival وI enjoyed it."]},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"Our Day at the Rose Festival","body":"Last spring, my family and I visited the Taif Rose Festival. We arrived early in the morning.\nThe fields looked colorful, and the air smelled wonderful. We walked between the rose bushes and watched the farmers. They picked thousands of pink roses!\nMy little brother tried rose ice cream, and he loved it. Mom decorated our picnic mat with petals.\nIn the afternoon, we visited a rose factory and learned how people make rose water. We stayed until sunset.\nIt was a day to remember!","word_count":85,"audio_id":"AUD-GV-L03-U2-LS1-T1"}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L03-U2-LS1-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"Yesterday, we ___ our grandparents.","options":["visit","visits","visited","are visit"],"answer":"visited","explanation":"Past time word → past simple.","explanation_ar":"كلمات الماضي ← الماضي البسيط."},{"q":"My sister ___ a delicious cake on Friday.","options":["bake","baked","bakes","bakeed"],"answer":"baked","explanation":"Verb ends in e → add -d.","explanation_ar":"الفعل المنتهي بـ e نضيف له d."},{"q":"Last night, Omar ___ the football match.","options":["watched","watch","is watched","watches"],"answer":"watched","explanation":"Past time word → past simple.","explanation_ar":"كلمات الماضي ← الماضي البسيط."},{"q":"The children ___ the classroom for Eid.","options":["decorates","decorated","decorateed","decorate"],"answer":"decorated","explanation":"Verb ends in e → add -d.","explanation_ar":"الفعل المنتهي بـ e نضيف له d."},{"q":"","options":["He is played chess with his uncle.","He play chess with his uncle yesterday.","He playeds chess with his uncle.","He played chess with his uncle."],"answer":"He played chess with his uncle.","explanation":"The past form is the same for all subjects (no -s).","explanation_ar":"الماضي لا يتغير مع الضمائر."},{"q":"We ___ at the hotel at noon.","options":["arrived","are arrived","arrive","arriveed"],"answer":"arrived","explanation":"Verb ends in e → add -d.","explanation_ar":"الفعل المنتهي بـ e نضيف له d."}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U2-LS1-B1","type":"gap_fill","instructions":"Guided practice: Write the past form. Word bank: enjoyed, cleaned, parked","items":[{"q":"Last week, I ______ (clean) my room.","options":[],"answer":"cleaned","explanation":"Regular verbs: add -ed for the past.","explanation_ar":"الأفعال المنتظمة: نضيف ed."},{"q":"The guests ______ (enjoy) the food.","options":[],"answer":"enjoyed","explanation":"Regular verbs: add -ed for the past.","explanation_ar":"الأفعال المنتظمة: نضيف ed."},{"q":"My dad ______ (park) the car near the gate.","options":[],"answer":"parked","explanation":"Regular verbs: add -ed for the past.","explanation_ar":"الأفعال المنتظمة: نضيف ed."}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U2-LS1-B2","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Change the sentences to the past.","items":[{"q":"I help my brother. (yesterday)  (past)","options":[],"answer":"I helped my brother yesterday.","explanation":"Past time word → past simple.","explanation_ar":"كلمات الماضي ← الماضي البسيط."},{"q":"She opens the gift. (last night)  (past)","options":[],"answer":"She opened the gift last night.","explanation":"The past form is the same for all subjects (no -s).","explanation_ar":"الماضي لا يتغير مع الضمائر."},{"q":"They walk to the park. (on Friday)  (past)","options":[],"answer":"They walked to the park on Friday.","explanation":"Regular verbs: add -ed for the past.","explanation_ar":"الأفعال المنتظمة: نضيف ed."}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U2-LS1-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Write about yesterday.","items":[{"q":"Yesterday morning, I ___.","options":[],"answer":"Yesterday morning, I prayed Fajr with my dad.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses past simple affirmative of regular verbs (verb + -ed) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Yesterday after lunch, I ___.","options":[],"answer":"Yesterday after lunch, I played football.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses past simple affirmative of regular verbs (verb + -ed) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Last night, my family ___.","options":[],"answer":"Last night, my family watched a film.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses past simple affirmative of regular verbs (verb + -ed) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Last Friday, we ___.","options":[],"answer":"Last Friday, we visited my aunt.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses past simple affirmative of regular verbs (verb + -ed) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Two days ago, I ___.","options":[],"answer":"Two days ago, I finished a new book.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses past simple affirmative of regular verbs (verb + -ed) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U2-LS1-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: A special day.","items":[{"q":"Write 4 sentences about a special day with regular past verbs.","options":[],"answer":"Last Eid, we visited our grandparents. We decorated the house. We played games. We enjoyed the food.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses past simple affirmative of regular verbs (verb + -ed) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 sentences about what your friend did last weekend (ask him).","options":[],"answer":"Faisal stayed at home. He watched a match.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses past simple affirmative of regular verbs (verb + -ed) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Underline the past verbs in your sentences. Count them.","options":[],"answer":"visited, decorated, played, enjoyed – 4 verbs","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses past simple affirmative of regular verbs (verb + -ed) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Grammar Hot Seat","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["One student from each team sits in the hot seat facing the class.","The teacher shows a cue card behind the student; the team gives a clue using past simple affirmative of regular verbs (verb + -ed) without saying the word.","The student in the hot seat guesses the cue word within 30 seconds.","Teams score 1 point for a correct guess and 1 point for a correct clue sentence. Rotate seats."],"data":[{"label":"visited"},{"label":"played"},{"label":"watched"},{"label":"cooked"},{"label":"arrived"},{"label":"stayed"},{"label":"helped"},{"label":"walked"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"I ___ my homework last night.","options":["finish","finished","finishes","am finished"],"answer":"finished","explanation":"Past time word → past simple.","explanation_ar":"كلمات الماضي ← الماضي البسيط."},{"q":"She ___ the gift with blue paper.","options":["wraps","wraped","wrapped","wrap"],"answer":"wrapped","explanation":"Regular verbs: add -ed for the past.","explanation_ar":"الأفعال المنتظمة: نضيف ed."},{"q":"They ___ in Jeddah last summer.","options":["stayed","stayes","are stayed","stay"],"answer":"stayed","explanation":"Past time word → past simple.","explanation_ar":"كلمات الماضي ← الماضي البسيط."},{"q":"","options":["We celebrateed Grandma's birthday.","We celebrate Grandma's birthday last week.","We are celebrated Grandma's birthday.","We celebrated Grandma's birthday."],"answer":"We celebrated Grandma's birthday.","explanation":"Verb ends in e → add -d.","explanation_ar":"الفعل المنتهي بـ e نضيف له d."},{"q":"","options":["My cousin love the boat trip yesterday.","My cousin loveds the boat trip.","My cousin is loved the boat trip.","My cousin loved the boat trip."],"answer":"My cousin loved the boat trip.","explanation":"The past form is the same for all subjects (no -s).","explanation_ar":"الماضي لا يتغير مع الضمائر."},{"q":"Two days ago, it ___ all afternoon.","options":["rain","is rained","rained","rains"],"answer":"rained","explanation":"Past time word → past simple.","explanation_ar":"كلمات الماضي ← الماضي البسيط."},{"q":"The farmer ___ the roses carefully.","options":["picked","picks","pick","is picked"],"answer":"picked","explanation":"Regular verbs: add -ed for the past.","explanation_ar":"الأفعال المنتظمة: نضيف ed."},{"q":"","options":["Dad washs the car on Friday.","Dad is washed the car on Friday.","Dad washed the car on Friday.","Dad washeds the car on Friday."],"answer":"Dad washed the car on Friday.","explanation":"Don't use am/is/are/was with a past simple verb.","explanation_ar":"لا نضع be مع الفعل الماضي."},{"q":"We ___ the museum in 2023.","options":["are visit","visited","visiting","visit"],"answer":"visited","explanation":"Past time word → past simple.","explanation_ar":"كلمات الماضي ← الماضي البسيط."},{"q":"","options":["The teacher thankeds us.","The teacher thanked us.","The teacher thanks us yesterday.","The teacher was thank us."],"answer":"The teacher thanked us.","explanation":"The past form is the same for all subjects (no -s).","explanation_ar":"الماضي لا يتغير مع الضمائر."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L03-U2-LS1-IMG01","prompt":"Lina's family walking through pink rose fields at the Taif Rose Festival, farmers picking roses, her little brother eating rose ice cream. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Lina's family walking through pink rose fields at the Taif Rose Festival, farmers picking roses, her little brother eating rose ice cream"},{"id":"GV-L03-U2-LS1-IMG02","prompt":"clean background panel for a grammar box about past simple affirmative of regular verbs (verb + -ed), with Zaki the Falcon pointing at a blank board on the right; leave large empty space for text overlay. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"clean background panel for a grammar box about past simple affirmative of regular verbs (verb + -ed), with Zaki the Falcon pointing at a blank board on the right"},{"id":"GV-L03-U2-LS1-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows trip (a short journey to a place and back); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing trip: a short journey to a place and back"},{"id":"GV-L03-U2-LS1-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows picnic (a meal you eat outside, in a park or the countryside); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing picnic: a meal you eat outside, in a park or the countryside"},{"id":"GV-L03-U2-LS1-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows festival (a special time when people celebrate something); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing festival: a special time when people celebrate something"},{"id":"GV-L03-U2-LS1-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows visit (to go to see a place or a person); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing visit: to go to see a place or a person"},{"id":"GV-L03-U2-LS1-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Grammar Hot Seat”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Grammar Hot Seat"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L03-U2-LS1-W01","script":"trip. trip. Our class trip was to the science center.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L03-U2-LS1-W02","script":"picnic. picnic. We had a picnic under the trees.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L03-U2-LS1-W03","script":"festival. festival. The date festival in Buraidah is famous.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L03-U2-LS1-W04","script":"visit. visit. We visited our cousins in Jeddah.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L03-U2-LS1-T1","script":"Last spring, my family and I visited the Taif Rose Festival. We arrived early in the morning. The fields looked colorful, and the air smelled wonderful. We walked between the rose bushes and watched the farmers. They picked thousands of pink roses! My little brother tried rose ice cream, and he loved it. Mom decorated our picnic mat with petals. In the afternoon, we visited a rose factory and learned how people make rose water. We stayed until sunset. It was a day to remember!","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L03-U2-LS1-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “We Visited the Rose Festival: Past Simple Regular Verbs”. Let’s learn past simple affirmative of regular verbs (verb + -ed) together. Listen to the start of “Our Day at the Rose Festival”: Last spring, my family and I visited the Taif Rose Festival. We arrived early in the morning. Look at the green words. We use the past simple for actions that started and finished in the past: We visited the festival last spring. For regular verbs, add -ed to the base verb: visit → visited, walk → walked. The past form is the same for every subject: I visited, she visited, they visited. Here are some examples. I helped my mom yesterday. We celebrated Eid at Grandpa's house. The guests arrived at nine. Be careful! Some learners say: “Yesterday I visit my uncle.” That’s not right. We say: “Yesterday I visited my uncle.” yesterday → past → -ed. Quick check: \"We visited the festival last spring.\" Is the visit finished? … Think! … Yes – it's in the past. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"We visited the festival\" and \"I enjoyed it\".","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.9"}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U2-LS2","title":"Yesterday, Last Week, Two Days Ago: Past Time Expressions","objectives":["Students will be able to use past time expressions correctly (yesterday, last, ago).","Students will be able to put time expressions at the start (with a comma) or at the end of a sentence.","I can say \"last week\", \"two days ago\" and \"in 2020\".","I can put time words in the right place."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام تعابير الزمن الماضي بشكل صحيح.","سيتمكن الطلاب من وضع تعبير الزمن في بداية الجملة (مع فاصلة) أو في نهايتها.","أستطيع أن أقول last week وtwo days ago وin 2020.","أستطيع أن أضع كلمات الزمن في مكانها الصحيح."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"arrive","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ɚˈaɪv/","definition":"to get to a place","arabic":"يصل","example":"The guests arrived at eight o'clock.","image_id":"GV-L03-U2-LS2-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L03-U2-LS2-W01"},{"word":"celebrate","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ˈsɛləˌbreɪt/","definition":"to do something enjoyable for a special day","arabic":"يحتفل","example":"We celebrated Grandpa's birthday.","image_id":"GV-L03-U2-LS2-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L03-U2-LS2-W02"},{"word":"decorate","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ˈdɛkɚˌeɪt/","definition":"to make something look beautiful with things like flowers or lights","arabic":"يزيّن","example":"The children decorated the classroom for Eid.","image_id":"GV-L03-U2-LS2-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L03-U2-LS2-W03"},{"word":"enjoy","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ˌɛnˈdʒɔɪ/","definition":"to like doing something very much","arabic":"يستمتع","example":"I enjoyed the boat ride.","image_id":"GV-L03-U2-LS2-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L03-U2-LS2-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"Past time expressions tell us when something happened: yesterday, yesterday morning, last night, last week, last year, two days ago, in 2020, on Friday.\nUse last with no the: last Friday (NOT the last Friday). Use ago after the time: three weeks ago.\nTime expressions usually go at the end: We visited Abha last year. They can go at the start with a comma: Last year, we visited Abha.","examples":["I called my grandma yesterday.","We moved to Taif in 2021.","Last night, the wind was very strong.","The new mall opened two months ago.","My cousins arrived on Thursday.","Yesterday afternoon, we played basketball.","The school trip was last month.","I started karate a year ago."],"common_errors":["✗ I visited my uncle before two days. → ✓ I visited my uncle two days ago. (Use … ago.)","✗ We played football in last Friday. → ✓ We played football last Friday. (No in or the before last.)","✗ Yesterday night I watched a film. → ✓ Last night, I watched a film. (We say last night.)","✗ Last week we cooked kabsa. → ✓ Last week, we cooked kabsa. (Comma after a time phrase at the start.)"],"arabic":"تعابير الزمن الماضي: yesterday (أمس) وlast week (الأسبوع الماضي) وtwo days ago (قبل يومين) وin 2020.\nلا نقول in last week أو the last week، بل last week فقط.\nنقول two days ago وليس before two days، ونقول last night وليس yesterday night.\nإذا بدأنا الجملة بتعبير الزمن نضع بعده فاصلة."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Yesterday, Last Week, Two Days Ago: Past Time Expressions”. Let’s learn past time expressions (yesterday, last…, … ago, in + year, on + day) and their position together.","on_screen":"GV-L03-U2-LS2 | Yesterday, Last Week, Two Days Ago: Past Time Expressions","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Remember these patterns: We visited Abha last year. • Two days ago, I cleaned my room. I didn't go out yesterday. (Unit 3) When did you visit Abha? – Last year. (Unit 3)","on_screen":"We visited Abha last year. • Two days ago, I cleaned my room. | I didn't go out yesterday. (Unit 3) | When did you visit Abha? – Last year. (Unit 3)","visual":"Pattern strips slide in from the left; the key words are highlighted in Leaf Green."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Past time expressions tell us when something happened: yesterday, yesterday morning, last night, last week, last year, two days ago, in 2020, on Friday. Use last with no the: last Friday (NOT the last Friday). Use ago after the time: three weeks ago.","on_screen":"past time expressions (yesterday, last…, … ago, in + year, on + day) and their position","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. I called my grandma yesterday. We moved to Taif in 2021. Last night, the wind was very strong.","on_screen":"I called my grandma yesterday. / We moved to Taif in 2021. / Last night, the wind was very strong.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “I visited my uncle before two days.” That’s not right. We say: “I visited my uncle two days ago.” Use … ago.","on_screen":"✗ I visited my uncle before two days.   ✓ I visited my uncle two days ago.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: Is \"last night\" the same as \"yesterday night\"? … Think! … We say *last night*, not yesterday night. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"last week\", \"two days ago\" and \"in 2020\".","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can say \"last week\", \"two days ago\" and \"in 2020\".","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: past time expressions (yesterday, last…, … ago, in + year, on + day) and their position.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","تعابير الزمن الماضي: yesterday (أمس) وlast week (الأسبوع الماضي) وtwo days ago (قبل يومين) وin 2020.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: I visited my uncle before two days. — الصحيح: I visited my uncle two days ago.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أقول last week وtwo days ago وin 2020."]},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L03-U2-LS2-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"We visited Al-Ula two years ___.","options":["last","past","before","ago"],"answer":"ago","explanation":"number + time + ago.","explanation_ar":"العدد ثم الوقت ثم ago."},{"q":"I talked to my cousin ___.","options":["yesterday night","last night","in last night","the last night"],"answer":"last night","explanation":"Say last night, not yesterday night.","explanation_ar":"نقول last night."},{"q":"My family moved to Riyadh ___ 2019.","options":["last","at","in","on"],"answer":"in","explanation":"in + year / month.","explanation_ar":"in مع السنة والشهر."},{"q":"We played tennis ___ Saturday.","options":["last","the last","in last","ago"],"answer":"last","explanation":"last + week/month/year/Friday (no the, no in).","explanation_ar":"last بدون the أو in."},{"q":"","options":["Last month, we visited the zoo.","In last month, we visited the zoo.","Last month we, visited the zoo.","Last, month we visited the zoo."],"answer":"Last month, we visited the zoo.","explanation":"Time phrase at the start → comma.","explanation_ar":"فاصلة بعد تعبير الزمن في البداية."},{"q":"The shop opened ___ ago.","options":["in three weeks","the three weeks","three weeks","last three weeks"],"answer":"three weeks","explanation":"number + time + ago.","explanation_ar":"العدد ثم الوقت ثم ago."}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U2-LS2-B1","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Rewrite with ago.","items":[{"q":"I watched the match. (the match was 3 days before today)  (ago)","options":[],"answer":"I watched the match three days ago.","explanation":"number + time + ago.","explanation_ar":"العدد ثم الوقت ثم ago."},{"q":"We moved house. (one year before now)  (ago)","options":[],"answer":"We moved house a year ago.","explanation":"number + time + ago.","explanation_ar":"العدد ثم الوقت ثم ago."},{"q":"She cleaned the kitchen. (one hour before now)  (ago)","options":[],"answer":"She cleaned the kitchen an hour ago.","explanation":"number + time + ago.","explanation_ar":"العدد ثم الوقت ثم ago."}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U2-LS2-B2","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Move the time expression to the start. Add a comma.","items":[{"q":"We stayed at home yesterday.  (start)","options":[],"answer":"Yesterday, we stayed at home.","explanation":"Time phrase at the start → comma.","explanation_ar":"فاصلة بعد تعبير الزمن في البداية."},{"q":"My dad washed the car last Friday.  (start)","options":[],"answer":"Last Friday, my dad washed the car.","explanation":"Time phrase at the start → comma.","explanation_ar":"فاصلة بعد تعبير الزمن في البداية."},{"q":"They opened a new park in 2024.  (start)","options":[],"answer":"In 2024, they opened a new park.","explanation":"Time phrase at the start → comma.","explanation_ar":"فاصلة بعد تعبير الزمن في البداية."}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U2-LS2-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Make a timeline of your life.","items":[{"q":"In ___, I was born.","options":[],"answer":"In 2016, I was born.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses past time expressions (yesterday, last…, … ago, in + year, on + day) and their position correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"___ years ago, I started school.","options":[],"answer":"Four years ago, I started school.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses past time expressions (yesterday, last…, … ago, in + year, on + day) and their position correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Last year, I ___.","options":[],"answer":"Last year, I learned to swim.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses past time expressions (yesterday, last…, … ago, in + year, on + day) and their position correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Last month, my family ___.","options":[],"answer":"Last month, my family visited Madinah.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses past time expressions (yesterday, last…, … ago, in + year, on + day) and their position correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Yesterday, I ___.","options":[],"answer":"Yesterday, I helped my grandpa in the garden.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses past time expressions (yesterday, last…, … ago, in + year, on + day) and their position correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U2-LS2-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: My week diary.","items":[{"q":"Write 4 diary sentences about last week. Start 2 with a time phrase and a comma.","options":[],"answer":"Last Sunday, I started a new book. I played chess on Tuesday. On Thursday, we visited my uncle. I cleaned my bike yesterday.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses past time expressions (yesterday, last…, … ago, in + year, on + day) and their position correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Ask a partner \"What did you do last weekend?\" Write 2 of his answers.","options":[],"answer":"He visited his grandpa. He played football on Saturday.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses past time expressions (yesterday, last…, … ago, in + year, on + day) and their position correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one sentence with \"ago\" and one with \"in\" + a year.","options":[],"answer":"We traveled to Egypt two years ago. My brother was born in 2020.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses past time expressions (yesterday, last…, … ago, in + year, on + day) and their position correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Sentence Builder Race","mechanic":"sentence_builder","rules":["Each team receives the same tile set.","In 5 minutes, build as many different correct sentences as possible using past time expressions (yesterday, last…, … ago, in + year, on + day) and their position.","Write each sentence on the team sheet.","Swap sheets with another team to check. One point per correct sentence; no points for repeats."],"data":[{"cue":"we / visit / the farm / last Friday"},{"cue":"I / play / football / yesterday"},{"cue":"my sister / bake / a cake / on Eid"},{"cue":"they / arrive / late / last night"},{"cue":"Dad / wash / the car / two days ago"},{"cue":"we / stay / in Abha / last summer"},{"cue":"Omar / help / his grandma / yesterday"},{"cue":"the baby / cry / all night / last week"},{"cue":"I / watch / a match / on Thursday"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"I finished the book ___.","options":["before","ago","last","yesterday"],"answer":"yesterday","explanation":"Say last night, not yesterday night.","explanation_ar":"نقول last night."},{"q":"My uncle arrived ten minutes ___.","options":["last","past","ago","before"],"answer":"ago","explanation":"number + time + ago.","explanation_ar":"العدد ثم الوقت ثم ago."},{"q":"We painted the house ___ year.","options":["last","ago","in last","the last"],"answer":"last","explanation":"last + week/month/year/Friday (no the, no in).","explanation_ar":"last بدون the أو in."},{"q":"","options":["I phoned my aunt last night.","I phoned my aunt yesterday night.","I phoned my aunt the last night.","I phoned my aunt in last night."],"answer":"I phoned my aunt last night.","explanation":"Say last night, not yesterday night.","explanation_ar":"نقول last night."},{"q":"The museum opened ___ 2018.","options":["at","in","ago","on"],"answer":"in","explanation":"in + year / month.","explanation_ar":"in مع السنة والشهر."},{"q":"","options":["Three days ago, we planted a tree.","Before three days, we planted a tree.","Three days ago we, planted a tree.","Ago three days, we planted a tree."],"answer":"Three days ago, we planted a tree.","explanation":"number + time + ago.","explanation_ar":"العدد ثم الوقت ثم ago."},{"q":"","options":["Last Thursday Lina visited, her teacher.","In last Thursday, Lina visited her teacher.","Last Thursday, Lina visited her teacher.","The last Thursday Lina visited her teacher."],"answer":"Last Thursday, Lina visited her teacher.","explanation":"Time phrase at the start → comma.","explanation_ar":"فاصلة بعد تعبير الزمن في البداية."},{"q":"We traveled to Malaysia ___.","options":["the last summer","last summer","in last summer","summer last"],"answer":"last summer","explanation":"last + week/month/year/Friday (no the, no in).","explanation_ar":"last بدون the أو in."},{"q":"","options":["ago a week","a week before ago","before a week","a week ago"],"answer":"a week ago","explanation":"number + time + ago.","explanation_ar":"العدد ثم الوقت ثم ago."},{"q":"","options":["The yesterday afternoon, it rained.","Yesterday afternoon it, rained.","Yesterday afternoon, it rained.","In yesterday afternoon, it rained."],"answer":"Yesterday afternoon, it rained.","explanation":"Time phrase at the start → comma.","explanation_ar":"فاصلة بعد تعبير الزمن في البداية."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L03-U2-LS2-IMG01","prompt":"A timeline on the board with sticky notes: \"in 2024 – moved house\", \"last month – school trip\", \"two days ago – picnic\", \"yesterday – science test\", Zaki pointing along the line. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"A timeline on the board with sticky notes: \"in 2024 – moved house\", \"last month – school trip\", \"two days ago – picnic\", \"yesterday – science test\", Zaki pointing along the line"},{"id":"GV-L03-U2-LS2-IMG02","prompt":"two-panel visual contrasting correct and incorrect use of past time expressions (yesterday, last…, … ago, in + year, on + day) and their position: a green tick panel and a soft red cross panel with simple objects from the theme “A Day to Remember”; empty space for text overlay. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"two-panel visual contrasting correct and incorrect use of past time expressions (yesterday, last…, … ago, in + year, on + day) and their position: a green tick panel and a soft red cross panel with simple objects from the theme “A Day to Remember”"},{"id":"GV-L03-U2-LS2-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows arrive (to get to a place); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing arrive: to get to a place"},{"id":"GV-L03-U2-LS2-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows celebrate (to do something enjoyable for a special day); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing celebrate: to do something enjoyable for a special day"},{"id":"GV-L03-U2-LS2-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows decorate (to make something look beautiful with things like flowers or lights); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing decorate: to make something look beautiful with things like flowers or lights"},{"id":"GV-L03-U2-LS2-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows enjoy (to like doing something very much); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing enjoy: to like doing something very much"},{"id":"GV-L03-U2-LS2-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Sentence Builder Race”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Sentence Builder Race"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L03-U2-LS2-W01","script":"arrive. arrive. The guests arrived at eight o'clock.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L03-U2-LS2-W02","script":"celebrate. celebrate. We celebrated Grandpa's birthday.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L03-U2-LS2-W03","script":"decorate. decorate. The children decorated the classroom for Eid.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L03-U2-LS2-W04","script":"enjoy. enjoy. I enjoyed the boat ride.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L03-U2-LS2-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Yesterday, Last Week, Two Days Ago: Past Time Expressions”. Let’s learn past time expressions (yesterday, last…, … ago, in + year, on + day) and their position together. Remember these patterns: We visited Abha last year. • Two days ago, I cleaned my room. I didn't go out yesterday. (Unit 3) When did you visit Abha? – Last year. (Unit 3) Past time expressions tell us when something happened: yesterday, yesterday morning, last night, last week, last year, two days ago, in 2020, on Friday. Use last with no the: last Friday (NOT the last Friday). Use ago after the time: three weeks ago. Here are some examples. I called my grandma yesterday. We moved to Taif in 2021. Last night, the wind was very strong. Be careful! Some learners say: “I visited my uncle before two days.” That’s not right. We say: “I visited my uncle two days ago.” Use … ago. Quick check: Is \"last night\" the same as \"yesterday night\"? … Think! … We say *last night*, not yesterday night. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"last week\", \"two days ago\" and \"in 2020\".","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.9"}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U2-LS3","title":"Colorful and Wonderful: Event Words and the Suffix -ful","objectives":["Students will be able to use words for trips, festivals and celebrations.","Students will be able to form and understand adjectives with -ful (= full of).","I can talk about trips and celebrations.","I can make words like \"colorful\" and \"helpful\"."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام كلمات الرحلات والمهرجانات والاحتفالات.","سيتمكن الطلاب من تكوين صفات بلاحقة ful وفهمها.","أستطيع أن أتحدث عن الرحلات والاحتفالات.","أستطيع أن أكوّن كلمات مثل colorful وhelpful."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"gift","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ɡɪft/","definition":"something you give to someone; a present","arabic":"هدية","example":"Lina wrapped a gift for her mother.","image_id":"GV-L03-U2-LS3-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L03-U2-LS3-W01"},{"word":"wonderful","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈwʌndɚfəl/","definition":"very, very good","arabic":"رائع","example":"The fireworks were wonderful!","image_id":"GV-L03-U2-LS3-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L03-U2-LS3-W02"},{"word":"colorful","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈkʌlɚfəl/","definition":"with many bright colors","arabic":"ملوّن","example":"The market was full of colorful lanterns.","image_id":"GV-L03-U2-LS3-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L03-U2-LS3-W03"},{"word":"peaceful","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈpisfəl/","definition":"quiet and calm","arabic":"هادئ / مسالم","example":"The beach was peaceful in the morning.","image_id":"GV-L03-U2-LS3-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L03-U2-LS3-W04"},{"word":"careful","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈkɛrfəl/","definition":"thinking about what you do so you are safe","arabic":"حذر / حريص","example":"Be careful near the water!","image_id":"GV-L03-U2-LS3-W05","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L03-U2-LS3-W05"}],"explanation":{"text":"Event words help us tell about special days: trip, picnic, festival, gift, celebrate, decorate, visit, enjoy.\nThe suffix -ful means full of. Add it to a noun to make an adjective: color + ful = colorful (full of color), help + ful = helpful, peace + ful = peaceful.\nSpelling: -ful has only one l. If the noun ends in consonant + y, change y → i: beauty → beautiful.\nWord families: color: colorful (adj), colorfully (adv), colors (n) | help: helper (n), helpful (adj), helpfully (adv) | peace: peaceful (adj), peacefully (adv) | care: careful (adj), carefully (adv), careless (adj) | beauty: beautiful (adj), beautifully (adv)\nCollocations/phrases: go on a trip • have a picnic • celebrate Eid • decorate the house • give a gift • enjoy the day","examples":["We went on a trip to the mountains.","The festival had music and food stalls.","My mom was very helpful at the school fair.","The lanterns were colorful.","The desert is peaceful at night.","Be careful with the hot tea!","We celebrated National Day in the park.","Sara gave her teacher a gift."],"common_errors":["✗ The flowers were very colorfull. → ✓ The flowers were very colorful. (-ful has one l.)","✗ The view was beautyful. → ✓ The view was beautiful. (beauty → beauti + ful.)","✗ We made a picnic. → ✓ We had a picnic. (We have a picnic.)","✗ Thank you, you are very help. → ✓ Thank you, you are very helpful. (Use the adjective helpful.)"],"arabic":"اللاحقة ful تعني «مليء بـ»: color + ful = colorful (ملوّن).\nful تُكتب بحرف l واحد فقط: colorful وليس colorfull.\nإذا انتهت الكلمة بحرف ساكن + y نحوّلها إلى i: beauty → beautiful.\nنقول have a picnic وليس make a picnic."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Colorful and Wonderful: Event Words and the Suffix -ful”. Let’s learn trip and event vocabulary; adjectives with the suffix -ful together.","on_screen":"GV-L03-U2-LS3 | Colorful and Wonderful: Event Words and the Suffix -ful","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Meet some new words. gift: something you give to someone; a present. wonderful: very, very good. colorful: with many bright colors.","on_screen":"gift | wonderful | colorful","visual":"Each word card flips over to show its picture (vocabulary image briefs) and Arabic meaning."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Event words help us tell about special days: trip, picnic, festival, gift, celebrate, decorate, visit, enjoy. The suffix -ful means full of. Add it to a noun to make an adjective: color + ful = colorful (full of color), help + ful = helpful, peace + ful = peaceful.","on_screen":"trip and event vocabulary; adjectives with the suffix -ful","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. We went on a trip to the mountains. The festival had music and food stalls. My mom was very helpful at the school fair.","on_screen":"We went on a trip to the mountains. / The festival had music and food stalls. / My mom was very helpful at the school fair.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “The flowers were very colorfull.” That’s not right. We say: “The flowers were very colorful.” -ful has one l.","on_screen":"✗ The flowers were very colorfull.   ✓ The flowers were very colorful.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: What does \"peaceful\" mean? … Think! … Full of peace – quiet and calm. Great job! Now you can say: I can talk about trips and celebrations.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can talk about trips and celebrations.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: trip and event vocabulary; adjectives with the suffix -ful.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","اللاحقة ful تعني «مليء بـ»: color + ful = colorful (ملوّن).","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: The flowers were very colorfull. — الصحيح: The flowers were very colorful.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أتحدث عن الرحلات والاحتفالات."]},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L03-U2-LS3-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct word.","items":[{"q":"The market had many bright colors. It was ___.","options":["colorly","colorfull","colorful","colored full"],"answer":"colorful","explanation":"noun + -ful = adjective meaning \"full of\".","explanation_ar":"الاسم + ful = صفة بمعنى «مليء بـ»."},{"q":"Thank you for your help. You are very ___.","options":["helpful","helping full","helpfull","helply"],"answer":"helpful","explanation":"-ful has only one l.","explanation_ar":"ful بحرف l واحد."},{"q":"The garden was quiet and calm. It was ___.","options":["peaceful","peacefull","peacing","peacely"],"answer":"peaceful","explanation":"noun + -ful = adjective meaning \"full of\".","explanation_ar":"الاسم + ful = صفة بمعنى «مليء بـ»."},{"q":"The view from the mountain was ___.","options":["beautyful","beautiful","beautly","beautifull"],"answer":"beautiful","explanation":"consonant + y → i + ful (beautiful).","explanation_ar":"y تتحول إلى i."},{"q":"On Friday, we ___ a picnic in the park.","options":["did","had","went","made"],"answer":"had","explanation":"Use the right word partner: have a picnic, go on a trip.","explanation_ar":"الكلمات المترافقة."},{"q":"We ___ the house with lights for Eid.","options":["arrived","celebrated","visited","decorated"],"answer":"decorated","explanation":"Choose the event word that fits.","explanation_ar":"اختر كلمة المناسبة."}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U2-LS3-B1","type":"match","instructions":"Guided practice: Match the word to the meaning.","items":[{"q":"careful","options":["a meal outside","thinking about safety","get to a place","a special time of celebration","a present","very, very good"],"answer":"thinking about safety","explanation":"careful → thinking about safety. noun + -ful = adjective meaning \"full of\".","explanation_ar":"الاسم + ful = صفة بمعنى «مليء بـ»."},{"q":"wonderful","options":["a meal outside","thinking about safety","get to a place","a special time of celebration","a present","very, very good"],"answer":"very, very good","explanation":"wonderful → very, very good. noun + -ful = adjective meaning \"full of\".","explanation_ar":"الاسم + ful = صفة بمعنى «مليء بـ»."},{"q":"festival","options":["a meal outside","thinking about safety","get to a place","a special time of celebration","a present","very, very good"],"answer":"a special time of celebration","explanation":"festival → a special time of celebration. noun + -ful = adjective meaning \"full of\".","explanation_ar":"الاسم + ful = صفة بمعنى «مليء بـ»."},{"q":"gift","options":["a meal outside","thinking about safety","get to a place","a special time of celebration","a present","very, very good"],"answer":"a present","explanation":"gift → a present. noun + -ful = adjective meaning \"full of\".","explanation_ar":"الاسم + ful = صفة بمعنى «مليء بـ»."},{"q":"arrive","options":["a meal outside","thinking about safety","get to a place","a special time of celebration","a present","very, very good"],"answer":"get to a place","explanation":"arrive → get to a place. noun + -ful = adjective meaning \"full of\".","explanation_ar":"الاسم + ful = صفة بمعنى «مليء بـ»."},{"q":"picnic","options":["a meal outside","thinking about safety","get to a place","a special time of celebration","a present","very, very good"],"answer":"a meal outside","explanation":"picnic → a meal outside. noun + -ful = adjective meaning \"full of\".","explanation_ar":"الاسم + ful = صفة بمعنى «مليء بـ»."}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U2-LS3-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Write about events you remember.","items":[{"q":"The most colorful place I visited was ___.","options":[],"answer":"The most colorful place I visited was the flower market.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses trip and event vocabulary; adjectives with the suffix -ful correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"A peaceful place I know is ___.","options":[],"answer":"A peaceful place I know is my grandpa's farm.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses trip and event vocabulary; adjectives with the suffix -ful correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Someone who is always helpful is ___.","options":[],"answer":"Someone who is always helpful is my big brother.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses trip and event vocabulary; adjectives with the suffix -ful correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Last year, we celebrated ___.","options":[],"answer":"Last year, we celebrated my uncle's wedding.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses trip and event vocabulary; adjectives with the suffix -ful correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"The best gift I got was ___.","options":[],"answer":"The best gift I got was a bike.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses trip and event vocabulary; adjectives with the suffix -ful correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U2-LS3-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Make a word-family tree.","items":[{"q":"Write the -ful adjective for: care, color, help, peace.","options":[],"answer":"careful, colorful, helpful, peaceful","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses trip and event vocabulary; adjectives with the suffix -ful correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 3 sentences about a festival with 3 -ful words.","options":[],"answer":"The festival was wonderful. The lights were colorful. The guides were helpful.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses trip and event vocabulary; adjectives with the suffix -ful correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one safety sentence with \"careful\".","options":[],"answer":"Be careful when you cross the street.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses trip and event vocabulary; adjectives with the suffix -ful correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Word Family Tree","mechanic":"drag_and_drop","rules":["Teams take turns drawing a word card.","Place the card on the correct branch of the tree and say a sentence with it.","Correct placement and sentence = 2 points.","The team with the most points when the tree is full wins."],"data":[{"word":"colorful","category":"adjective","family":"color"},{"word":"colorfully","category":"adverb","family":"color"},{"word":"colors","category":"noun","family":"color"},{"word":"helper","category":"noun","family":"help"},{"word":"helpful","category":"adjective","family":"help"},{"word":"helpfully","category":"adverb","family":"help"},{"word":"peaceful","category":"adjective","family":"peace"},{"word":"peacefully","category":"adverb","family":"peace"},{"word":"careful","category":"adjective","family":"care"},{"word":"carefully","category":"adverb","family":"care"},{"word":"careless","category":"adjective","family":"care"},{"word":"beautiful","category":"adjective","family":"beauty"},{"word":"beautifully","category":"adverb","family":"beauty"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"color + ful = ___","options":["colorfull","colourfull","colorful","colorfil"],"answer":"colorful","explanation":"-ful has only one l.","explanation_ar":"ful بحرف l واحد."},{"q":"beauty + ful = ___","options":["beautyful","beautful","beautifull","beautiful"],"answer":"beautiful","explanation":"consonant + y → i + ful (beautiful).","explanation_ar":"y تتحول إلى i."},{"q":"Please be ___ with the scissors.","options":["careful","caring","carefull","careless"],"answer":"careful","explanation":"noun + -ful = adjective meaning \"full of\".","explanation_ar":"الاسم + ful = صفة بمعنى «مليء بـ»."},{"q":"The night in the desert was ___.","options":["colorful","peacefull","helpful","peaceful"],"answer":"peaceful","explanation":"noun + -ful = adjective meaning \"full of\".","explanation_ar":"الاسم + ful = صفة بمعنى «مليء بـ»."},{"q":"We ___ a trip to Abha last summer.","options":["made","went on","did","had on"],"answer":"went on","explanation":"Use the right word partner: have a picnic, go on a trip.","explanation_ar":"الكلمات المترافقة."},{"q":"A present for someone is a ___.","options":["trip","picnic","gift","festival"],"answer":"gift","explanation":"Choose the event word that fits.","explanation_ar":"اختر كلمة المناسبة."},{"q":"The guests ___ at seven.","options":["celebrated","arrived","enjoyed","decorated"],"answer":"arrived","explanation":"Choose the event word that fits.","explanation_ar":"اختر كلمة المناسبة."},{"q":"The fireworks were very, very good. They were ___.","options":["wonderful","careful","helpful","peaceful"],"answer":"wonderful","explanation":"noun + -ful = adjective meaning \"full of\".","explanation_ar":"الاسم + ful = صفة بمعنى «مليء بـ»."},{"q":"Which word means \"full of help\"?","options":["helper","helpful","helping","helpless"],"answer":"helpful","explanation":"noun + -ful = adjective meaning \"full of\".","explanation_ar":"الاسم + ful = صفة بمعنى «مليء بـ»."},{"q":"We ___ Grandma's 70th birthday last week.","options":["picnicked","arrived","visited at","celebrated"],"answer":"celebrated","explanation":"Choose the event word that fits.","explanation_ar":"اختر كلمة المناسبة."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L03-U2-LS3-IMG01","prompt":"A Saudi National Day celebration in a park: colorful green flags, families having a picnic, children decorating with balloons and a peaceful sunset. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"A Saudi National Day celebration in a park: colorful green flags, families having a picnic, children decorating with balloons and a peaceful sunset"},{"id":"GV-L03-U2-LS3-IMG02","prompt":"word-web visual: a central circle with branches to 5 small picture icons of the lesson words; empty labels. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"word-web visual: a central circle with branches to 5 small picture icons of the lesson words"},{"id":"GV-L03-U2-LS3-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows gift (something you give to someone; a present); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing gift: something you give to someone; a present"},{"id":"GV-L03-U2-LS3-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows wonderful (very, very good); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing wonderful: very, very good"},{"id":"GV-L03-U2-LS3-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows colorful (with many bright colors); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing colorful: with many bright colors"},{"id":"GV-L03-U2-LS3-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows peaceful (quiet and calm); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing peaceful: quiet and calm"},{"id":"GV-L03-U2-LS3-W05","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows careful (thinking about what you do so you are safe); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing careful: thinking about what you do so you are safe"},{"id":"GV-L03-U2-LS3-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Word Family Tree”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Word Family Tree"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L03-U2-LS3-W01","script":"gift. gift. Lina wrapped a gift for her mother.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L03-U2-LS3-W02","script":"wonderful. wonderful. The fireworks were wonderful!","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L03-U2-LS3-W03","script":"colorful. colorful. The market was full of colorful lanterns.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L03-U2-LS3-W04","script":"peaceful. peaceful. The beach was peaceful in the morning.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L03-U2-LS3-W05","script":"careful. careful. Be careful near the water!","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L03-U2-LS3-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Colorful and Wonderful: Event Words and the Suffix -ful”. Let’s learn trip and event vocabulary; adjectives with the suffix -ful together. Meet some new words. gift: something you give to someone; a present. wonderful: very, very good. colorful: with many bright colors. Event words help us tell about special days: trip, picnic, festival, gift, celebrate, decorate, visit, enjoy. The suffix -ful means full of. Add it to a noun to make an adjective: color + ful = colorful (full of color), help + ful = helpful, peace + ful = peaceful. Here are some examples. We went on a trip to the mountains. The festival had music and food stalls. My mom was very helpful at the school fair. Be careful! Some learners say: “The flowers were very colorfull.” That’s not right. We say: “The flowers were very colorful.” -ful has one l. Quick check: What does \"peaceful\" mean? … Think! … Full of peace – quiet and calm. Great job! Now you can say: I can talk about trips and celebrations.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.9"}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U2-LS4","title":"Played, Liked, Stopped, Tried: Spelling -ed","objectives":["Students will be able to spell regular past verbs with -ed, -d, double consonant + -ed and -ied.","Students will be able to correct -ed spelling mistakes in a recount.","I can spell \"stopped\", \"tried\" and \"liked\".","I can fix -ed spelling mistakes."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من تهجئة الأفعال الماضية المنتظمة بإضافة ed أو d أو مضاعفة الحرف أو ied.","سيتمكن الطلاب من تصحيح أخطاء تهجئة ed في نص سردي.","أستطيع أن أتهجّى stopped وtried وliked.","أستطيع أن أصحح أخطاء تهجئة ed."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"trip","pos":"noun","ipa":"/trɪp/","definition":"a short journey to a place and back","arabic":"رحلة","example":"Our class trip was to the science center.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"picnic","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈpɪkˌnɪk/","definition":"a meal you eat outside, in a park or the countryside","arabic":"نزهة / رحلة طعام","example":"We had a picnic under the trees.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"festival","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈfɛstəvəl/","definition":"a special time when people celebrate something","arabic":"مهرجان","example":"The date festival in Buraidah is famous.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"visit","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ˈvɪzɪt/","definition":"to go to see a place or a person","arabic":"يزور","example":"We visited our cousins in Jeddah.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"arrive","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ɚˈaɪv/","definition":"to get to a place","arabic":"يصل","example":"The guests arrived at eight o'clock.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"celebrate","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ˈsɛləˌbreɪt/","definition":"to do something enjoyable for a special day","arabic":"يحتفل","example":"We celebrated Grandpa's birthday.","image_id":"","audio_id":""}],"explanation":{"text":"Most verbs add -ed: walk → walked, visit → visited.\nVerbs ending in e add only -d: like → liked, arrive → arrived.\nShort verbs with one vowel + one consonant double the consonant: stop → stopped, plan → planned. Consonant + y → ied: try → tried, study → studied. But vowel + y → -ed: play → played, enjoy → enjoyed.\n+ ed: watched, cleaned, helped\ne → + d: smiled, decorated, danced\none vowel + one consonant → double + ed: stopped, hugged, planned\nconsonant + y → ied: cried, carried, studied • vowel + y → ed: stayed, played","examples":["The bus stopped at the gate.","We planned a surprise party.","The baby cried all night.","Grandma smiled at the photos.","We stayed at a farm.","Faisal carried the heavy box.","My sister studied for her test.","They danced the ardah at the festival."],"common_errors":["✗ stoped → ✓ stopped (Double the p.)","✗ tryed → ✓ tried (consonant + y → ied.)","✗ plaied → ✓ played (vowel + y → just ed.)","✗ likeed → ✓ liked (Verb ends in e → add d.)"],"arabic":"معظم الأفعال نضيف لها ed: walked.\nالفعل المنتهي بـ e نضيف له d فقط: liked.\nالفعل القصير (متحرك + ساكن) نضاعف آخره: stopped. والساكن + y يصبح ied: tried، أما المتحرك + y فنضيف ed: played."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Played, Liked, Stopped, Tried: Spelling -ed”. Let’s learn spelling rules for the past simple -ed together.","on_screen":"GV-L03-U2-LS4 | Played, Liked, Stopped, Tried: Spelling -ed","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Most verbs add -ed: walk → walked, visit → visited.","on_screen":"spelling rules for the past simple -ed","visual":"Pattern strips slide in from the left; the key words are highlighted in Leaf Green."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Most verbs add -ed: walk → walked, visit → visited. Verbs ending in e add only -d: like → liked, arrive → arrived.","on_screen":"+ ed: watched, cleaned, helped • e → + d: smiled, decorated, danced • one vowel + one consonant → double + ed: stopped, hugged, planned","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. The bus stopped at the gate. We planned a surprise party. The baby cried all night.","on_screen":"The bus stopped at the gate. / We planned a surprise party. / The baby cried all night.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “stoped.” That’s not right. We say: “stopped.” Double the p.","on_screen":"✗ stoped   ✓ stopped","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: Why is it \"played\" but \"tried\"? … Think! … *play* has a vowel before y; *try* has a consonant before y. Great job! Now you can say: I can spell \"stopped\", \"tried\" and \"liked\".","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can spell \"stopped\", \"tried\" and \"liked\".","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: spelling rules for the past simple -ed.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","معظم الأفعال نضيف لها ed: walked.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: stoped — الصحيح: stopped","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أتهجّى stopped وtried وliked."]},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"Our Camping Trip (editing passage)","body":"Last winter, we planed a camping trip. We arriveed at the desert in the afternoon. My dad carryed the tent. We plaied football and watchd the stars. It was wonderful!","word_count":30,"audio_id":""}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L03-U2-LS4-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct spelling.","items":[{"q":"shop → ___","options":["shopped","shopeed","shoped","shoppd"],"answer":"shopped","explanation":"One vowel + one consonant → double + ed.","explanation_ar":"نضاعف الحرف الأخير."},{"q":"try → ___","options":["tryed","triyed","tryied","tried"],"answer":"tried","explanation":"Consonant + y → ied.","explanation_ar":"ساكن + y ← ied."},{"q":"enjoy → ___","options":["enjoied","enjoyyed","enjoyed","enjoyd"],"answer":"enjoyed","explanation":"Vowel + y → ed.","explanation_ar":"متحرك + y ← ed."},{"q":"smile → ___","options":["smileed","smiled","smild","smilled"],"answer":"smiled","explanation":"Ends in e → + d.","explanation_ar":"ينتهي بـ e ← نضيف d."},{"q":"plan → ___","options":["planeed","plannd","planned","planed"],"answer":"planned","explanation":"One vowel + one consonant → double + ed.","explanation_ar":"نضاعف الحرف الأخير."},{"q":"watch → ___","options":["watched","watcheed","watchd","watchted"],"answer":"watched","explanation":"Most verbs: + ed.","explanation_ar":"معظم الأفعال: نضيف ed."}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U2-LS4-B1","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Correct the spelling mistake.","items":[{"q":"The car stoped at the red light.","options":[],"answer":"The car stopped at the red light.","explanation":"stoped → stopped. One vowel + one consonant → double + ed.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: stoped → stopped. نضاعف الحرف الأخير."},{"q":"My brother carryed my bag.","options":[],"answer":"My brother carried my bag.","explanation":"carryed → carried. Consonant + y → ied.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: carryed → carried. ساكن + y ← ied."},{"q":"We plaied in the snow.","options":[],"answer":"We played in the snow.","explanation":"plaied → played. Vowel + y → ed.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: plaied → played. متحرك + y ← ed."},{"q":"She decorateed the cake.","options":[],"answer":"She decorated the cake.","explanation":"decorateed → decorated. Ends in e → + d.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: decorateed → decorated. ينتهي بـ e ← نضيف d."},{"q":"The puppy huged my leg!","options":[],"answer":"The puppy hugged my leg!","explanation":"huged → hugged. One vowel + one consonant → double + ed.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: huged → hugged. نضاعف الحرف الأخير."},{"q":"They studyed all evening.","options":[],"answer":"They studied all evening.","explanation":"studyed → studied. Consonant + y → ied.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: studyed → studied. ساكن + y ← ied."}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U2-LS4-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Edit Ziyad's recount.","items":[{"q":"Last winter, we planed a camping trip.","options":[],"answer":"Last winter, we planned a camping trip.","explanation":"planed → planned. Most verbs: + ed.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: planed → planned. معظم الأفعال: نضيف ed."},{"q":"We arriveed at the desert in the afternoon.","options":[],"answer":"We arrived at the desert in the afternoon.","explanation":"arriveed → arrived. Most verbs: + ed.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: arriveed → arrived. معظم الأفعال: نضيف ed."},{"q":"My dad carryed the tent.","options":[],"answer":"My dad carried the tent.","explanation":"carryed → carried. Most verbs: + ed.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: carryed → carried. معظم الأفعال: نضيف ed."},{"q":"We plaied football and watched the stars.","options":[],"answer":"We played football and watched the stars.","explanation":"plaied → played. Most verbs: + ed.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: plaied → played. معظم الأفعال: نضيف ed."},{"q":"We played football and watchd the stars.","options":[],"answer":"We played football and watched the stars.","explanation":"watchd → watched. Most verbs: + ed.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: watchd → watched. معظم الأفعال: نضيف ed."}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U2-LS4-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write with -ed verbs.","items":[{"q":"Write one past verb for each rule: +ed, +d, double, ied.","options":[],"answer":"helped, liked, stopped, cried","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses spelling rules for the past simple -ed correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 3 sentences about a trip with -ed verbs.","options":[],"answer":"We visited a farm. We fed the camels. We enjoyed the fresh milk.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses spelling rules for the past simple -ed correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Swap with a partner. Check his -ed spelling. Write one correction.","options":[],"answer":"\"plaied\" → \"played\"","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses spelling rules for the past simple -ed correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Spelling Relay","mechanic":"word_builder","rules":["Teams line up facing the board.","The teacher says a word; the first student runs to the board and writes the first letter.","The next student adds the next letter, and so on.","The first team with the correct spelling wins the point."],"data":[{"word":"visited","clue":""},{"word":"arrived","clue":""},{"word":"stopped","clue":""},{"word":"planned","clue":""},{"word":"tried","clue":""},{"word":"carried","clue":""},{"word":"enjoyed","clue":""},{"word":"played","clue":""},{"word":"smiled","clue":""},{"word":"studied","clue":""},{"word":"trip","clue":"a short journey to a place and back"},{"word":"picnic","clue":"a meal you eat outside, in a park or the countryside"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"hug → ___","options":["huggd","hugeed","hugged","huged"],"answer":"hugged","explanation":"One vowel + one consonant → double + ed.","explanation_ar":"نضاعف الحرف الأخير."},{"q":"cry → ___","options":["cryied","cried","cryed","criyed"],"answer":"cried","explanation":"Consonant + y → ied.","explanation_ar":"ساكن + y ← ied."},{"q":"stay → ___","options":["stayed","staied","stayyed","stayd"],"answer":"stayed","explanation":"Vowel + y → ed.","explanation_ar":"متحرك + y ← ed."},{"q":"dance → ___","options":["danceed","dancced","dancd","danced"],"answer":"danced","explanation":"Ends in e → + d.","explanation_ar":"ينتهي بـ e ← نضيف d."},{"q":"","options":["We claped at the end of the show.","We clapeed at the end of the show.","We clappd at the end of the show.","We clapped at the end of the show."],"answer":"We clapped at the end of the show.","explanation":"One vowel + one consonant → double + ed.","explanation_ar":"نضاعف الحرف الأخير."},{"q":"","options":["She hurryed to the bus stop.","She hurriied to the bus stop.","She hurried to the bus stop.","She hurried to the bus stopp."],"answer":"She hurried to the bus stop.","explanation":"Consonant + y → ied.","explanation_ar":"ساكن + y ← ied."},{"q":"","options":["They enjoyed the picnic.","They enjoied the picnic.","They enjoyeed the picnic.","They enjoyd the picnic."],"answer":"They enjoyed the picnic.","explanation":"Vowel + y → ed.","explanation_ar":"متحرك + y ← ed."},{"q":"Which spelling is wrong?","options":["skipped","skiped","hopped","dropped"],"answer":"skiped","explanation":"One vowel + one consonant → double + ed.","explanation_ar":"نضاعف الحرف الأخير."},{"q":"","options":["My uncle arrived late.","My uncle arriveed late.","My uncle arrivd late.","My uncle arrivved late."],"answer":"My uncle arrived late.","explanation":"Ends in e → + d.","explanation_ar":"ينتهي بـ e ← نضيف d."},{"q":"study → ___","options":["studeed","studyed","studied","studdied"],"answer":"studied","explanation":"Consonant + y → ied.","explanation_ar":"ساكن + y ← ied."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L03-U2-LS4-IMG01","prompt":"Two or three of the programme characters in a scene about “A Day to Remember” that shows spelling rules for the past simple -ed in action. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Two or three of the programme characters in a scene about “A Day to Remember” that shows spelling rules for the past simple -ed in action"},{"id":"GV-L03-U2-LS4-IMG02","prompt":"friendly editing-desk scene: a magnifying glass over a page with highlighted punctuation marks, Zaki holding a green pen. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"friendly editing-desk scene: a magnifying glass over a page with highlighted punctuation marks, Zaki holding a green pen"},{"id":"GV-L03-U2-LS4-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Spelling Relay”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Spelling Relay"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L03-U2-LS4-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Played, Liked, Stopped, Tried: Spelling -ed”. Let’s learn spelling rules for the past simple -ed together. Most verbs add -ed: walk → walked, visit → visited. Most verbs add -ed: walk → walked, visit → visited. Verbs ending in e add only -d: like → liked, arrive → arrived. Here are some examples. The bus stopped at the gate. We planned a surprise party. The baby cried all night. Be careful! Some learners say: “stoped.” That’s not right. We say: “stopped.” Double the p. Quick check: Why is it \"played\" but \"tried\"? … Think! … *play* has a vowel before y; *try* has a consonant before y. Great job! Now you can say: I can spell \"stopped\", \"tried\" and \"liked\".","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.9"}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U2-LS5","title":"A Day to Remember: Language in Use","objectives":["Students will be able to tell a partner about a memorable day.","Students will be able to write a recount in the past simple with time expressions and correct -ed spelling.","I can tell about a day to remember.","I can write a recount of a special day."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من إخبار زميل عن يوم لا يُنسى.","سيتمكن الطلاب من كتابة نص سردي بالماضي البسيط مع تعابير الزمن وتهجئة ed صحيحة.","أستطيع أن أحكي عن يوم لا يُنسى.","أستطيع أن أكتب نصًا سرديًا عن يوم مميز."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"trip","pos":"noun","ipa":"/trɪp/","definition":"a short journey to a place and back","arabic":"رحلة","example":"Our class trip was to the science center.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"picnic","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈpɪkˌnɪk/","definition":"a meal you eat outside, in a park or the countryside","arabic":"نزهة / رحلة طعام","example":"We had a picnic under the trees.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"festival","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈfɛstəvəl/","definition":"a special time when people celebrate something","arabic":"مهرجان","example":"The date festival in Buraidah is famous.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"visit","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ˈvɪzɪt/","definition":"to go to see a place or a person","arabic":"يزور","example":"We visited our cousins in Jeddah.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"arrive","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ɚˈaɪv/","definition":"to get to a place","arabic":"يصل","example":"The guests arrived at eight o'clock.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"celebrate","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ˈsɛləˌbreɪt/","definition":"to do something enjoyable for a special day","arabic":"يحتفل","example":"We celebrated Grandpa's birthday.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"decorate","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ˈdɛkɚˌeɪt/","definition":"to make something look beautiful with things like flowers or lights","arabic":"يزيّن","example":"The children decorated the classroom for Eid.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"enjoy","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ˌɛnˈdʒɔɪ/","definition":"to like doing something very much","arabic":"يستمتع","example":"I enjoyed the boat ride.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"gift","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ɡɪft/","definition":"something you give to someone; a present","arabic":"هدية","example":"Lina wrapped a gift for her mother.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"wonderful","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈwʌndɚfəl/","definition":"very, very good","arabic":"رائع","example":"The fireworks were wonderful!","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"colorful","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈkʌlɚfəl/","definition":"with many bright colors","arabic":"ملوّن","example":"The market was full of colorful lanterns.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"peaceful","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈpisfəl/","definition":"quiet and calm","arabic":"هادئ / مسالم","example":"The beach was peaceful in the morning.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"careful","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈkɛrfəl/","definition":"thinking about what you do so you are safe","arabic":"حذر / حريص","example":"Be careful near the water!","image_id":"","audio_id":""}],"explanation":{"text":"Today you use all of Unit 2: regular past verbs, time expressions, event words, -ful adjectives and -ed spelling.\nA recount tells what happened in order. It answers: When? Where? Who? What happened? How did you feel?\n✔ past simple: verb + -ed for finished actions\n✔ when: last…, … ago, in…, on…\n✔ order words: first, then, in the afternoon, in the evening\n✔ -ful adjectives and correct -ed spelling","examples":["Last Eid, we visited Makkah.","First, we prayed at the mosque.","Then we walked to a restaurant.","The streets were colorful and busy.","In the evening, we watched the lights.","My little brother cried when we left!","We stayed there for three days.","Everyone was helpful and kind."],"common_errors":["✗ Last year we visit Abha. → ✓ Last year, we visited Abha. (Past verb + comma after the time phrase.)","✗ The lights were colorfull. → ✓ The lights were colorful. (One l.)","✗ We plaied games. → ✓ We played games. (vowel + y → ed.)"],"arabic":"نراجع الماضي البسيط والأفعال المنتظمة وتعابير الزمن وكلمات المناسبات وتهجئة ed.\nالنص السردي يجيب: متى؟ أين؟ مَن؟ ماذا حدث؟ كيف شعرت؟\nاستخدم كلمات الترتيب first وthen وin the evening."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “A Day to Remember: Language in Use”. Let’s learn past simple regular verbs, time expressions, event words and -ed spelling (unit review) together.","on_screen":"GV-L03-U2-LS5 | A Day to Remember: Language in Use","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Let’s use everything from this unit. Your task: Memory circle: in groups, each student shows a photo or drawing of a special day and tells 4 sentences about it with past verbs and time words. Listeners ask one question each.","on_screen":"Language in use","visual":"Split screen: two cast members talking, with speech bubbles appearing."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Today you use all of Unit 2: regular past verbs, time expressions, event words, -ful adjectives and -ed spelling. A recount tells what happened in order. It answers: When? Where? Who? What happened? How did you feel?","on_screen":"✔ past simple: verb + -ed for finished actions • ✔ when: last…, … ago, in…, on… • ✔ order words: first, then, in the afternoon, in the evening","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. Last Eid, we visited Makkah. First, we prayed at the mosque. Then we walked to a restaurant.","on_screen":"Last Eid, we visited Makkah. / First, we prayed at the mosque. / Then we walked to a restaurant.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “Last year we visit Abha.” That’s not right. We say: “Last year, we visited Abha.” Past verb + comma after the time phrase.","on_screen":"✗ Last year we visit Abha.   ✓ Last year, we visited Abha.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: what is wrong with “The lights were colorfull.”? … Think! … It should be “The lights were colorful.”. Great job! Now you can say: I can tell about a day to remember.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can tell about a day to remember.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: past simple regular verbs, time expressions, event words and -ed spelling (unit review).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","نراجع الماضي البسيط والأفعال المنتظمة وتعابير الزمن وكلمات المناسبات وتهجئة ed.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: Last year we visit Abha. — الصحيح: Last year, we visited Abha.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أحكي عن يوم لا يُنسى."]},"texts":[{"type":"model","title":"National Day in the Park – Omar","body":"Last September, my family celebrated Saudi National Day in King Fahd Park.\nWe arrived at four o'clock. The park looked wonderful with green flags everywhere.\nMy cousins and I painted our faces green and white. We played games and watched a show.\nIn the evening, we enjoyed fireworks over the lake. They were so colorful!\nI loved every minute of that day. It was a day to remember!","word_count":68,"audio_id":"AUD-GV-L03-U2-LS5-T1"}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L03-U2-LS5-A1","type":"true_false","instructions":"Controlled practice: Read Omar's recount. True or False?","items":[{"q":"Omar's family celebrated National Day in a park.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “National Day in the Park – Omar”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"They arrived at seven o'clock.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “National Day in the Park – Omar”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Omar painted his face green and white.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “National Day in the Park – Omar”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"They watched fireworks in the morning.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “National Day in the Park – Omar”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Omar thought the fireworks were colorful.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “National Day in the Park – Omar”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Omar didn't enjoy the day.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “National Day in the Park – Omar”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U2-LS5-B1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Guided practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"Omar and his cousins ___ games in the park.","options":["are played","play","played","plaied"],"answer":"played","explanation":"Past simple: verb + -ed.","explanation_ar":"الماضي البسيط: الفعل + ed."},{"q":"They celebrated National Day last ___.","options":["ago","before","yesterday","September"],"answer":"September","explanation":"Past time expression (last…, … ago, in…).","explanation_ar":"تعابير الزمن الماضي."},{"q":"The fireworks were so ___.","options":["colorful","colorfull","color","colorly"],"answer":"colorful","explanation":"-ful adjective (one l).","explanation_ar":"صفة ful بحرف l واحد."},{"q":"In the evening, they ___ fireworks.","options":["enjoied","enjoyed","enjoy","enjoyd"],"answer":"enjoyed","explanation":"Check the -ed spelling rule.","explanation_ar":"تحقق من تهجئة ed."},{"q":"The park ___ wonderful.","options":["looked","is looked","lookd","looks"],"answer":"looked","explanation":"Past simple: verb + -ed.","explanation_ar":"الماضي البسيط: الفعل + ed."},{"q":"We ___ our faces for the celebration.","options":["celebrated","arrived","visited","painted"],"answer":"painted","explanation":"Choose the right event word.","explanation_ar":"اختر كلمة المناسبة الصحيحة."}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U2-LS5-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Memory circle. Write your notes.","items":[{"q":"When was your special day?","options":[],"answer":"It was two years ago, in spring.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses past simple regular verbs, time expressions, event words and -ed spelling (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Where were you?","options":[],"answer":"I was at my grandpa's farm in Al-Ahsa.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses past simple regular verbs, time expressions, event words and -ed spelling (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"What did you do? Write 2 past verbs.","options":[],"answer":"We picked dates and played with the goats.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses past simple regular verbs, time expressions, event words and -ed spelling (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"How did you feel?","options":[],"answer":"I felt very happy and excited.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses past simple regular verbs, time expressions, event words and -ed spelling (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one question a friend asked you, and your answer.","options":[],"answer":"Did you ride a camel? – Yes, I did!","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses past simple regular verbs, time expressions, event words and -ed spelling (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U2-LS5-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write \"A Day to Remember\".","items":[{"q":"Plan: when, where, who, 4 actions, a feeling.","options":[],"answer":"last Eid; Madinah; my family; prayed, visited, walked, enjoyed; peaceful and happy","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses past simple regular verbs, time expressions, event words and -ed spelling (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write your recount in 6–7 sentences.","options":[],"answer":"Last Eid, my family visited Madinah. We arrived in the morning. First, we prayed at the Prophet's Mosque. Then we walked around the city. The streets were colorful. We enjoyed dinner together. It was a peaceful, happy day.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses past simple regular verbs, time expressions, event words and -ed spelling (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Check: -ed spelling? time expressions? commas? Fix one mistake.","options":[],"answer":"I changed \"plaied\" to \"played\".","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses past simple regular verbs, time expressions, event words and -ed spelling (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Board Race Review","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["One student from each team stands at the board.","The teacher says a cue word and a task (meaning, spelling or sentence with past simple regular verbs, time expressions, event words and -ed spelling (unit review)).","The first correct answer wins a point; rotate players every round.","Play 10 rounds."],"data":[{"cue":"trip","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"picnic","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"festival","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"visit","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"arrive","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"celebrate","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"decorate","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"enjoy","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"gift","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"wonderful","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"colorful","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"peaceful","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"careful","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"Last week, my class ___ the science museum.","options":["visit","visits","is visited","visited"],"answer":"visited","explanation":"Past simple: verb + -ed.","explanation_ar":"الماضي البسيط: الفعل + ed."},{"q":"We moved to this house four years ___.","options":["before","ago","last","past"],"answer":"ago","explanation":"Past time expression (last…, … ago, in…).","explanation_ar":"تعابير الزمن الماضي."},{"q":"The nurse was kind and ___.","options":["helply","help","helpfull","helpful"],"answer":"helpful","explanation":"-ful adjective (one l).","explanation_ar":"صفة ful بحرف l واحد."},{"q":"My little sister ___ when she fell.","options":["cryied","criyed","cried","cryed"],"answer":"cried","explanation":"Check the -ed spelling rule.","explanation_ar":"تحقق من تهجئة ed."},{"q":"","options":["Last Friday, we had a picnic.","Last Friday, we made a picnic.","In last Friday, we had a picnic.","Last Friday we, had a picnic."],"answer":"Last Friday, we had a picnic.","explanation":"Choose the right event word.","explanation_ar":"اختر كلمة المناسبة الصحيحة."},{"q":"The train ___ at the station at noon.","options":["stopd","stopped","stoped","stopeed"],"answer":"stopped","explanation":"Check the -ed spelling rule.","explanation_ar":"تحقق من تهجئة ed."},{"q":"","options":["We decorated the classroom with balloons.","We decorateed the classroom with balloons.","We are decorated the classroom with balloons.","We decorate the classroom with balloons yesterday."],"answer":"We decorated the classroom with balloons.","explanation":"Past simple: verb + -ed.","explanation_ar":"الماضي البسيط: الفعل + ed."},{"q":"___, we watched the sunset.","options":["Last","Before","In the evening","Ago"],"answer":"In the evening","explanation":"Past time expression (last…, … ago, in…).","explanation_ar":"تعابير الزمن الماضي."},{"q":"The beach was calm and quiet. It was ___.","options":["peaceful","careful","colorful","helpful"],"answer":"peaceful","explanation":"-ful adjective (one l).","explanation_ar":"صفة ful بحرف l واحد."},{"q":"Which sentence is best for a recount?","options":["Two days ago we celebrate my brother's graduation.","Two days ago, we celebrateed my brother's graduation.","Before two days, we celebrated my brother's graduation.","Two days ago, we celebrated my brother's graduation."],"answer":"Two days ago, we celebrated my brother's graduation.","explanation":"Past simple: verb + -ed.","explanation_ar":"الماضي البسيط: الفعل + ed."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L03-U2-LS5-IMG01","prompt":"Omar reading his recount aloud to the class, with a photo of his family celebrating National Day in green clothes. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Omar reading his recount aloud to the class, with a photo of his family celebrating National Day in green clothes"},{"id":"GV-L03-U2-LS5-IMG02","prompt":"two programme characters doing the speaking task about “A Day to Remember”, speech bubbles left empty. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"two programme characters doing the speaking task about “A Day to Remember”, speech bubbles left empty"},{"id":"GV-L03-U2-LS5-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Board Race Review”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Board Race Review"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L03-U2-LS5-T1","script":"Last September, my family celebrated Saudi National Day in King Fahd Park. We arrived at four o'clock. The park looked wonderful with green flags everywhere. My cousins and I painted our faces green and white. We played games and watched a show. In the evening, we enjoyed fireworks over the lake. They were so colorful! I loved every minute of that day. It was a day to remember!","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L03-U2-LS5-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “A Day to Remember: Language in Use”. Let’s learn past simple regular verbs, time expressions, event words and -ed spelling (unit review) together. Let’s use everything from this unit. Your task: Memory circle: in groups, each student shows a photo or drawing of a special day and tells 4 sentences about it with past verbs and time words. Listeners ask one question each. Today you use all of Unit 2: regular past verbs, time expressions, event words, -ful adjectives and -ed spelling. A recount tells what happened in order. It answers: When? Where? Who? What happened? How did you feel? Here are some examples. Last Eid, we visited Makkah. First, we prayed at the mosque. Then we walked to a restaurant. Be careful! Some learners say: “Last year we visit Abha.” That’s not right. We say: “Last year, we visited Abha.” Past verb + comma after the time phrase. Quick check: what is wrong with “The lights were colorfull.”? … Think! … It should be “The lights were colorful.”. Great job! Now you can say: I can tell about a day to remember.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.9"}]}],"unit_test":[{"q":"We ___ the camel race last Saturday.","options":["watch","are watched","watches","watched"],"answer":"watched","explanation":"Past time word → past simple.","explanation_ar":"كلمات الماضي ← الماضي البسيط."},{"q":"My mom ___ a big lunch for the guests.","options":["cookd","cooks","cooked","is cooked"],"answer":"cooked","explanation":"Regular verbs: add -ed for the past.","explanation_ar":"الأفعال المنتظمة: نضيف ed."},{"q":"","options":["He visit the mosque with his dad yesterday.","He visiteds the mosque with his dad.","He is visited the mosque with his dad.","He visited the mosque with his dad."],"answer":"He visited the mosque with his dad.","explanation":"The past form is the same for all subjects (no -s).","explanation_ar":"الماضي لا يتغير مع الضمائر."},{"q":"The guests ___ at the party at nine.","options":["arrived","arrive","arriveed","are arrived"],"answer":"arrived","explanation":"Verb ends in e → add -d.","explanation_ar":"الفعل المنتهي بـ e نضيف له d."},{"q":"","options":["They laugh at the funny film last night.","They are laughed at the funny film.","They laugheds at the funny film.","They laughed at the funny film."],"answer":"They laughed at the funny film.","explanation":"Don't use am/is/are/was with a past simple verb.","explanation_ar":"لا نضع be مع الفعل الماضي."},{"q":"We traveled to Dubai three years ___.","options":["last","ago","past","before"],"answer":"ago","explanation":"number + time + ago.","explanation_ar":"العدد ثم الوقت ثم ago."},{"q":"I spoke to Grandpa ___.","options":["yesterday night","in last night","last night","the last night"],"answer":"last night","explanation":"Say last night, not yesterday night.","explanation_ar":"نقول last night."},{"q":"My brother started university ___ 2025.","options":["last","at","in","on"],"answer":"in","explanation":"in + year / month.","explanation_ar":"in مع السنة والشهر."},{"q":"","options":["Last weekend we, cleaned the garden.","In last weekend, we cleaned the garden.","The last weekend we cleaned the garden.","Last weekend, we cleaned the garden."],"answer":"Last weekend, we cleaned the garden.","explanation":"Time phrase at the start → comma.","explanation_ar":"فاصلة بعد تعبير الزمن في البداية."},{"q":"","options":["an hour ago","before an hour","an hour before ago","ago an hour"],"answer":"an hour ago","explanation":"number + time + ago.","explanation_ar":"العدد ثم الوقت ثم ago."},{"q":"The streets were full of bright lights. They were ___.","options":["colorly","colorfull","colorful","careful"],"answer":"colorful","explanation":"noun + -ful = adjective meaning \"full of\".","explanation_ar":"الاسم + ful = صفة بمعنى «مليء بـ»."},{"q":"The man showed us the way. He was very ___.","options":["helpful","helpfull","helping","helpless"],"answer":"helpful","explanation":"-ful has only one l.","explanation_ar":"ful بحرف l واحد."},{"q":"The view of the sea was ___.","options":["beautifull","beautly","beautyful","beautiful"],"answer":"beautiful","explanation":"consonant + y → i + ful (beautiful).","explanation_ar":"y تتحول إلى i."},{"q":"Be ___ when you swim in the sea!","options":["peaceful","careful","carefull","colorful"],"answer":"careful","explanation":"noun + -ful = adjective meaning \"full of\".","explanation_ar":"الاسم + ful = صفة بمعنى «مليء بـ»."},{"q":"We ___ a picnic under the palm trees.","options":["had","made","did","gave"],"answer":"had","explanation":"Use the right word partner: have a picnic, go on a trip.","explanation_ar":"الكلمات المترافقة."},{"q":"Lina gave her grandmother a ___ on Eid.","options":["festival","trip","gift","picnic"],"answer":"gift","explanation":"Choose the event word that fits.","explanation_ar":"اختر كلمة المناسبة."},{"q":"drop → ___","options":["droped","dropped","dropeed","droppd"],"answer":"dropped","explanation":"One vowel + one consonant → double + ed.","explanation_ar":"نضاعف الحرف الأخير."},{"q":"carry → ___","options":["carried","carrid","carryied","carryed"],"answer":"carried","explanation":"Consonant + y → ied.","explanation_ar":"ساكن + y ← ied."},{"q":"","options":["We playyed video games.","We played video games.","We plaied video games.","We playd video games."],"answer":"We played video games.","explanation":"Vowel + y → ed.","explanation_ar":"متحرك + y ← ed."},{"q":"","options":["She bakkd cookies for us.","She baked cookies for us.","She bakeed cookies for us.","She bakd cookies for us."],"answer":"She baked cookies for us.","explanation":"Verb ends in e → add -d.","explanation_ar":"الفعل المنتهي بـ e نضيف له d."},{"q":"","options":["The teacher hurried to class.","The teacher hurriyed to class.","The teacher hurryed to class.","The teacher hurryd to class."],"answer":"The teacher hurried to class.","explanation":"Consonant + y → ied.","explanation_ar":"ساكن + y ← ied."},{"q":"Pick the best opening for a recount:","options":["Last summer my family visit Abha.","Before last summer, my family visited Abha.","Last summer, my family visited Abha.","Last summer, my family is visited Abha."],"answer":"Last summer, my family visited Abha.","explanation":"Time phrase at the start → comma.","explanation_ar":"فاصلة بعد تعبير الزمن في البداية."},{"q":"How can we fix it? \"yesterday we plaied in the park.\"","options":["yesterday, we played in the park.","Yesterday, we plaied in the park.","Yesterday we play in the park.","Yesterday, we played in the park."],"answer":"Yesterday, we played in the park.","explanation":"Vowel + y → ed.","explanation_ar":"متحرك + y ← ed."},{"q":"What did you do on the weekend? – ___","options":["I visitied my cousins in Jeddah.","I visited my cousins in Jeddah.","I visit my cousins in Jeddah.","I am visited my cousins in Jeddah."],"answer":"I visited my cousins in Jeddah.","explanation":"Past simple: verb + -ed.","explanation_ar":"الماضي البسيط: الفعل + ed."}],"theme_ar":"يوم لا يُنسى","essential_question_ar":"ما الذي يجعل يومًا مميزًا لدرجة أننا نتذكّره؟","can_do":"I can tell about a special day in the past using regular past verbs and time expressions.","can_do_ar":"أستطيع أن أتحدث عن يوم مميز في الماضي باستخدام الأفعال الماضية المنتظمة وتعابير الزمن."});
